{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgF8cTBYP44qzNN54FFf5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"prompt\": \"A square, purely nonrepresentational abstract painting that fills the entire canvas edge to edge, with no frame, border, wall, room, or gallery setting. Oil and cold wax on heavy linen, built from many layers. The left third is dense and turbulent: thick, impasto knife strokes of oxblood red, burnt orange and bruised violet pile over each other in short, urgent, overlapping gestures. Scraped-back passages show older layers of ochre and slate underneath. Toward the center the pressure breaks. A long, deliberate sweep of cool ultramarine and deep teal pulls across the surface in one confident dry-brush motion. It leaves ragged, feathered edges where the bristles skip, and it cuts through the warm turbulence. The right two-thirds opens into wide, quiet fields of pale grey-green and chalky off-white. They are thinly scumbled, so that faint ghosts of earlier marks show through like half-erased thoughts. A few small, sharp flecks of acid yellow-green and one narrow vertical sliver of near-black sit in the emptiness and create spatial tension. Fine, scratched sgraffito lines run in a loose, rhythmic cadence, some pulling toward the calm area and some pulling away. Contrast is strong between heavy and weightless, hot and cold, crowded and empty. The surface is richly textured, with ridges, drips, dragged paint and matte and glossy patches catching light unevenly. The mood is restless but steadily resolving, with an uneasy balance and a hard-won stillness. No recognizable objects, figures, faces, bodies, scenes, landscapes, horizons, machines, diagrams, symbols, icons, letters, numbers, or text.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":444,"cache_read_input_tokens":11890,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m